Subject: [test image only] Parse an already complete cursor report before reading ahead

BusyBox 1.37.0 read_key() can read all of ESC[1;5R while trying the
Ctrl-arrow key table. The cursor-report parser must examine those bytes
before another read, or it consumes the following command as an unknown
escape sequence. Keep all bytes, bounds, key mappings and timeouts unchanged.

--- a/libbb/read_key.c
+++ b/libbb/read_key.c
@@ -223,0 +224,4 @@
+	/* The known-key matcher may already have read a complete cursor report.
+	 * Recognize it before consuming any following user input.
+	 */
+	goto check_cursor_pos;
@@ -240,0 +245 @@
+ check_cursor_pos:
